INT. PRECINCT 9 - INTERVIEW ROOM - NIGHT

Cinderblock. A table bolted to the floor. A two-way mirror. A fluorescent tube with a wasp trapped inside it.

OFFICER TAMAR HAIM, 30s, in uniform, sits with a legal pad. Across from her, an UNKNOWN MAN, 40s, in a damp jacket, holds a paper cup he has not drunk from.

TAMAR
Name.

UNKNOWN MAN
You tell me.

TAMAR
That's not how this works.

UNKNOWN MAN
Then I'm waiting.

A radio on Tamar's shoulder crackles.

DISPATCH (V.O.)
(radio)
Unit Nine, prints came back on your guy.

Tamar thumbs the mic.

TAMAR
Go ahead, Dispatch.

DISPATCH (V.O.)
(radio)
Desmond Pryce. Forty-one. Two priors. Last known address, a storage unit off Route 6.

She glances at the man. He keeps his eyes on the table.

TAMAR
(to the man)
Mr. Pryce.

DESMOND
Don't.

TAMAR
That's your name?

DESMOND
It was my father's.

TAMAR
Mr. Pryce, why are you holding the cup?

DESMOND
Because my hands shake.

DISPATCH (V.O.)
(radio)
Unit Nine, also, the storage unit's been flagged. Smell reported.

Desmond sets the cup down very carefully.

TAMAR
What's in unit one-forty?

DESMOND
Nothing you want.

TAMAR
That isn't a no.
